===============================================================================
External Toolchain Boundaries & Operational Interfaces
===============================================================================

Vivisect interfaces with external electronic design automation (EDA) toolchains
that are not bundled or redistributed with this software:

  * AMD Vivado Design Suite:
    Vivisect provides Starlark build rules and orchestration wrappers that
    invoke host-installed AMD Vivado tools (such as xvlog, xelab, xsim, and
    vivado). Vivisect does not vendor or redistribute any AMD binaries, header
    files, or proprietary libraries. All trademarks and copyrights in AMD
    Vivado belong to Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.

  * Verilator:
    Vivisect provides build rules and test runners that execute the open-source
    Verilator compiler and link generated simulation harnesses against the
    Verilator C++ runtime (verilated.h) under the terms of the Verilator linking
    exception (LGPL-3.0 with static linking exception / Artistic License 2.0).
    Verilator is copyright its respective authors and contributors.

===============================================================================
Test Fixtures & Mock Vendor Data
===============================================================================

Unit test fixtures within this repository (e.g., in rules/test/timing_runner_test.py
and rules/support/test/run_isolated_test.py) contain synthetic mock tool log
outputs and vendor copyright strings (such as "Copyright 1986-2022 Xilinx, Inc.").
These strings are functional test data used solely to verify log parsing, error
trapping, and process isolation, and do not constitute redistribution of vendor
software or IP.
